--- verdict: does FW-CADIS flatten the error across the family? ---
   uniform   : max/min = 100.91 (95% CI [65.8, 160.3]), sd(log) = 1.543, cost = 1.96e+08
   FW-CADIS  : max/min = 287.30 (95% CI [194.7, 414.8]), sd(log) = 1.900, cost = 3.09e+07

   paired comparison (common random numbers): corr(pi_hat at shallowest threshold) = 0.062
      -> seed sharing bought ~no measurable correlation here (as the docstring warned it might not); the paired CI below is not meaningfully
         tighter than the independent one -- treat it as a sanity check, not a resolution.
   FW-CADIS - uniform (spread difference): +178.20 (95% CI [+59.8, +351.3])
      -> paired 95% CI EXCLUDES ZERO: FW-CADIS is LESS FLAT than uniform, resolved.
   coverage  : uniform 6/6,  FW-CADIS 6/6  <-- judged FIRST
   -> No flattening at this budget (CIs don't overlap -- FW-CADIS is
      measurably WORSE here). Either alpha is mistuned, or the ladder
      budget is too small for the deep bins to be served.
   NOTE: flatness is the metric here, NOT a single FOM. Comparing one
   threshold at a time is exactly what this stage is designed to replace.

